o workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["EVgo Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $576M market cap on $384M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +92% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Gross margins of 6% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The company is burning through $124M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -18.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (25.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 36% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u201